@startuml

title A chart reads a series: one live subscription, one history call

hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor "User" as u
participant "Client\n(chart)" as c
queue "NATS" as n
participant "Marketdata\nhistory read" as h
participant "Lane\nrecent window" as w
database "Tick table" as s

== The chart opens ==

u -> c : open the chart of a series
c -> n : subscribe\nmarketdata.v1.ops.market_tick.<tenant>.<party>.<type>.<series>.>
note right of c
  Subscribe first.
  The client buffers every live tick
  until the history reply arrives.
end note

c -> h : get_series_ticks(series, from, to)\nrequest/reply
h -> h : check session, tenant and party
h -> w : ticks from the window start to now
w --> h : ticks, with their coordinates
h -> s : ticks from "from" to the window start\none index probe on series and time
s --> h : ticks
h --> c : one reply\ncoordinates once, then time, coordinate and value arrays\nand the as_of time of the read

c -> c : merge history and buffered live ticks\nby coordinate and time, keep one of a pair
c -> u : plot the series

== The chart stays open ==

loop every conflated live tick
    n -> c : market_tick
    c -> c : add the tick to the series
    c -> u : extend the plot
end

== The connection drops and returns ==

c -> n : subscribe again
c -> h : get_series_ticks(series, from = newest held tick, to)
h --> c : one reply with the missed span
c -> c : merge by coordinate and time

== The user scrolls to an older span ==

u -> c : scroll back
c -> h : get_series_ticks(series, from, to = oldest held tick)
h --> c : one reply with the older span
c -> c : merge by coordinate and time
c -> u : plot the longer series

@enduml
